---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Stat from '../../components/Stat.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Kaye Putnam for Oncourse Home Solutions"
  description="A brief on why Kaye Putnam fits the Head of Brand Strategy role at Oncourse Home Solutions."
  noindex={true}
>
  <Nav />

  <main style="padding-top: var(--site-header-height);">

    <Section variant="default" size="lg">
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">Prepared for the Oncourse Home Solutions team</p>
      <h1 class="page-headline">Head of Brand Strategy, <em>with receipts</em>.</h1>
      <p style="max-width: 58ch; margin-top: var(--space-6); font-size: var(--text-lg);">
        I'm Kaye Putnam, a brand strategist and marketing leader in St. Charles, twenty minutes up the road from your Naperville office. Below, your role's requirements mapped to work I've already shipped.
      </p>
      <p style="max-width: 58ch; margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--gray-600);">
        (A personalized page for one specific account is exactly how I run partner and account-based marketing, so consider this a work sample too.)
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" size="md">
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-4);">
        <Stat variant="dark" value="$3.7M" label="ARR built from zero" />
        <Stat variant="dark" value="$190M+" label="Client revenue managed" />
        <Stat variant="dark" value="75+" label="Recurring-revenue clients" />
        <Stat variant="dark" value="250K+" label="Brand quiz takers" />
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="warm" size="lg">
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">The mapping</p>
      <h2 class="map-title">Your requirements, mapped to <em>shipped work</em>.</h2>

      <div class="evidence">
        <a class="shot" href="/work/freewyld-foundry" aria-label="Freewyld Foundry case study">
          <img src="/for/oncourse/foundry-home.png" alt="Freewyld Foundry website homepage" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="label">You asked for brand strategy across every stakeholder</p>
          <h3>A four-brand portfolio, built and stewarded</h3>
          <p>I lead brand strategy for a consumer hospitality brand, a B2B consultancy, and two founder personal brands, with the brand promise carried through every touchpoint of the customer journey.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Documented voice systems, guidelines, and messaging architecture for each brand</li>
            <li>Customer and partner value propositions defined, then activated from acquisition through onboarding, ongoing service, and renewal</li>
            <li>Built as part of the founding team: zero clients and zero revenue to 75+ clients and $3.7M ARR</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/work/freewyld-foundry">See the public case study →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="evidence evidence--flip">
        <a class="shot" href="/brand-archetypes" aria-label="Brand archetypes framework">
          <img src="/for/oncourse/kp-archetypes.png" alt="Brand archetypes framework page" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="label">You asked for practical, results-first brand thinking</p>
          <h3>A framework 250,000+ people have used</h3>
          <p>My psychology-driven archetype framework exists because brand strategy should move revenue. It has defined positioning, value propositions, and messaging for more than 100 companies across B2B, consumer, and service businesses.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>250,000+ quiz completions; featured in university classrooms and business conferences</li>
            <li>The practical output is always the same: a brand the whole company can execute consistently</li>
            <li>Deep experience translating brand strategy into segmentation and persona-level messaging</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/brand-archetypes">Explore the framework →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="evidence">
        <a class="shot" href="/work/brand-archetype-quiz" aria-label="Quiz rebuild case study">
          <img src="/for/oncourse/kp-quiz.png" alt="Natively rebuilt brand personality quiz" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="label">You asked how the brand shows up in AI search</p>
          <h3>AI-era discoverability, already in production</h3>
          <p>Your posting calls out optimizing how Oncourse is represented when customers research through AI tools. I have built exactly this: content systems designed for how AI assistants read, cite, and recommend brands.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Structured data across 25+ page types and a deliberate AI-crawler policy</li>
            <li>A documented answer-engine optimization playbook the whole content operation follows</li>
            <li>Three websites rebuilt with AI-assisted development; I treat AI as marketing infrastructure, not a delegated tool</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/quiz">Try the live build →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="evidence evidence--flip">
        <a class="shot" href="/work/freewyld-cabins" aria-label="Freewyld case study">
          <img src="/for/oncourse/freewyld-home.png" alt="Freewyld hospitality brand website" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="label">You asked for creative direction and journey activation</p>
          <h3>A consumer brand experience, end to end</h3>
          <p>I rebuilt the Freewyld guest experience from brand identity through booking flow to lifecycle email, directing creative across web, video, social, and email with one consistent voice.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Migrated and relaunched the site in one week on an AI-friendly foundation: architecture upgrades to tracking, speed, usability, and SEO</li>
            <li>Guest journey activated at every stage: booking, pre-arrival, in-stay upsell offers, and post-stay review requests across a 12-touch email lifecycle</li>
            <li>Consumer press earned along the way: Staycation TV feature and a Visit California mention</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/work/freewyld-cabins">See the public case study →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="default" size="md">
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-12);">
        <div>
          <h3 class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Storytelling &amp; earned media</h3>
          <p>20+ published client case studies with a per-client approval workflow. Founder placements on industry podcasts, VRMA speaking in 2025 and 2026, and a repeatable system for turning customer wins into brand credibility.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Partner marketing (B2B2C)</h3>
          <p>Co-created an 80-90 attendee industry event with partner Proper Insurance, then grew it into an ongoing content partnership: a joint podcast episode, coordinated blog content, and a dedicated partner page.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Teams &amp; creative leadership</h3>
          <p>Twelve years leading creative teams, from a core of three to project teams of fifteen. Today I lead marketing inside a 20-person company as part of its leadership team, with a hiring record my direct reports' reviews back up.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" size="lg">
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Thinking out loud</p>
      <h2 class="map-title" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-8);">A point of view on <em>your</em> brand.</h2>
      <p style="max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-8);">Three things I noticed in your posting that I'd want to explore in a first conversation.</p>
      <div class="pov-grid">
        <div>
          <h3 class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">The two-brand question</h3>
          <p>The American Water Resources to Oncourse decision reads like a renaming project, but the real work is sequencing customer and partner trust through the transition. I run a portfolio where brands share a family reputation while serving different buyers, and the architecture calls about what to share and what to separate shaped everything downstream.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Reviews are the brand surface</h3>
          <p>In home services, a prospect meets your Google and Trustpilot ratings before they meet any campaign, so reputation strategy and brand strategy are one discipline. I've built client advocacy systematically: case studies with approval workflows, review generation, and customer stories treated as a pipeline rather than a request.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Enrollment research is moving into AI</h3>
          <p>Your posting names how Oncourse is represented in AI tools during enrollment research, and that instinct is ahead of the market. I treat AI assistants as a distribution channel with its own ranking logic, and homeowner services is exactly the category where assistant recommendations will start deciding shortlists.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: var(--space-8); max-width: 58ch;">If any of these are live debates inside Oncourse, that's the conversation I'd most enjoy having.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="cream" size="lg">
      <h2 class="label" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">Let's talk</h2>
      <p style="max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
        The tailored resume below covers the full twenty years. I'd welcome a conversation about what brand strategy can do for Oncourse and American Water Resources.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/for/oncourse/Kaye-Putnam-Resume-Oncourse.pdf">Download my resume (PDF)</a><br />
        <a href="mailto:kayeputnam@gmail.com">kayeputnam@gmail.com</a><br />
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kayeputnam/">LinkedIn</a>
      </p>
    </Section>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .map-title {
    font-family: var(--ff-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-regular);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
  .evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: var(--space-10);
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-20);
  }
  .evidence:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .evidence--flip .shot {
    order: 2;
  }
  .shot img {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-300);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  }
  .shot {
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }
  .shot:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }
  .prose h3 {
    font-family: var(--ff-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
  }
  .prose ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .prose li::marker {
    color: var(--color-gold);
  }
  .pov-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-12);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .evidence {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }
    .evidence--flip .shot {
      order: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
